module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.Rename
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.FinitePresentation
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Operations
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.IntegralClosure.IsIntegralClosure.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Tower

/-!
# The approximating system of an integral algebra

Let `R → S` be an integral ring map. This file builds, from that data alone, an explicit
directed family of `R`-algebras which are simultaneously *finite as `R`-modules* and *of finite
presentation over `R`*, and which approximates `S`. The file
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/IntegralDirectedColimit/Colimit.lean` proves that the direct
limit of the family is `S`.

Together these give the commutative-algebra content of [Stacks, Tag 0817] -- the statement that
tag 0817 asserts for a quasi-coherent algebra on a scheme, read on a single affine open. Tag
0817 itself is a statement about sheaves of algebras and is *not* proved here.

## The construction

Everything happens inside the single polynomial ring `MvPolynomial S R`, on one variable `X x`
for each element `x` of `S`. Writing `eval` for the canonical surjection
`MvPolynomial S R → S` sending `X x` to `x`:

* `varSubalg R S s` is the subalgebra generated by the variables `X x` for `x ∈ s`;
* `annih R S x` is a chosen monic polynomial over `R` annihilating `x`, which exists because
  `S` is integral over `R`, and `rel R S x` is the resulting monic relation
  `(annih R S x)(X x)` inside the polynomial ring;
* an index `i : Index R S` is a finite set of variables together with a finite set of
  polynomial relations between them which already hold in `S`;
* `gens i` is the full relation set at `i`: the prescribed relations together with the monic
  relation on each chosen variable, and `obj i` is the quotient of `varSubalg R S i.1.1` by the
  ideal `relIdeal i` they generate.

Fixing one ambient polynomial ring is what makes the transition maps of the system trivial:
for `i ≤ j` the map `obj i → obj j` is induced by `Subalgebra.inclusion`, so no renaming of
variables occurs and functoriality is definitional. The two finiteness properties come from
the two halves of `gens i`: the monic relations make each variable integral in the quotient,
which gives module-finiteness, and the finiteness of `gens i` makes `relIdeal i` finitely
generated, which gives finite presentation.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.RingTheory.IntegralColimit.Index`: the index type of the approximating system.
* `Stacks.RingTheory.IntegralColimit.obj`: the approximating algebra at an index.
* `Stacks.RingTheory.IntegralColimit.varSubalg` and
  `Stacks.RingTheory.IntegralColimit.varSubalgEquiv`: the subalgebra generated by a set of
  variables, and its identification with the polynomial ring on that set.

## Main results

* `Stacks.RingTheory.IntegralColimit.Index.instIsDirectedOrder`: the index type is directed.
* `Stacks.RingTheory.IntegralColimit.moduleFinite_obj`: each approximating algebra is a finite
  `R`-module.
* `Stacks.RingTheory.IntegralColimit.finitePresentation_obj`: each approximating algebra is of
  finite presentation over `R`.

## Implementation notes

The index type is a subtype of `Set S × Set (MvPolynomial S R)` rather than a pair of
`Finset`s, so that no `DecidableEq` hypothesis on `S` is needed and the order is the product
order inherited from `Subtype.partialOrder`. The finiteness of the two components is carried
as part of the subtype predicate.

`relIdeal i` is spanned by `Subtype.val ⁻¹' gens i`, the preimage of the relation set inside
the subalgebra, rather than by a set constructed with membership proofs; since `Subtype.val` is
injective the preimage is finite, which is all that finite generation needs, and monotonicity
in `i` becomes the statement that `gens` is monotone.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0817](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0817)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 086N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/086N)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02JJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02JJ)
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

open MvPolynomial

universe u v

namespace Stacks.RingTheory.IntegralColimit

variable (R : Type u) (S : Type v) [CommRing R]

/-- The subalgebra of `MvPolynomial S R` generated by the variables indexed by `s`. -/
def varSubalg (s : Set S) : Subalgebra R (MvPolynomial S R) := Algebra.adjoin R (X '' s)

/-- The subalgebra generated by a set of variables is monotone in the set. -/
theorem varSubalg_mono {s t : Set S} (h : s ⊆ t) : varSubalg R S s ≤ varSubalg R S t :=
  Algebra.adjoin_mono (Set.image_mono h)

/-- The variable `X x` lies in the subalgebra generated by the variables indexed by `s` when
`x ∈ s`. -/
theorem X_mem_varSubalg {s : Set S} {x : S} (hx : x ∈ s) : X x ∈ varSubalg R S s :=
  Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩

/-- Renaming along the inclusion `s ↪ S` has image the subalgebra generated by the variables
indexed by `s`. -/
theorem range_rename_val (s : Set S) :
    (rename (Subtype.val : ↥s → S) : MvPolynomial ↥s R →ₐ[R] MvPolynomial S R).range
      = varSubalg R S s := by
  rw [varSubalg, rename_eq_aeval, ← Algebra.adjoin_range_eq_range_aeval]
  congr 1
  rw [Set.range_comp, Subtype.range_coe]

/-- The subalgebra generated by the variables indexed by `s` is the polynomial ring on `s`. -/
def varSubalgEquiv {s : Set S} : MvPolynomial ↥s R ≃ₐ[R] varSubalg R S s :=
  (AlgEquiv.ofInjective
      (rename (Subtype.val : ↥s → S) : MvPolynomial ↥s R →ₐ[R] MvPolynomial S R)
      (rename_injective _ Subtype.val_injective)).trans
    (Subalgebra.equivOfEq _ _ (range_rename_val R S s))

/-- The subalgebra generated by finitely many variables is of finite presentation. -/
theorem finitePresentation_varSubalg {s : Set S} (hs : s.Finite) :
    Algebra.FinitePresentation R (varSubalg R S s) := by
  have : Finite ↥s := hs.to_subtype
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation R (MvPolynomial ↥s R) :=
    Algebra.FinitePresentation.mvPolynomial_of_finitePresentation (A := R) ↥s
  exact Algebra.FinitePresentation.equiv (varSubalgEquiv R S)

variable [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]

/-- The canonical surjection from the polynomial ring on the elements of `S` onto `S`. -/
def eval : MvPolynomial S R →ₐ[R] S := aeval id

/-- `eval` sends the variable `X x` to `x`. -/
@[simp] theorem eval_X (x : S) : eval R S (X x) = x := by simp [eval]

/-- `eval` is surjective. -/
theorem eval_surjective : Function.Surjective (eval R S) := fun x => ⟨X x, eval_X R S x⟩

variable [Algebra.IsIntegral R S]

/-- A chosen monic polynomial over `R` annihilating `x`. -/
def annih (x : S) : Polynomial R := (Algebra.IsIntegral.isIntegral (R := R) x).choose

/-- The chosen annihilating polynomial of `x` is monic. -/
theorem annih_monic (x : S) : (annih R S x).Monic :=
  (Algebra.IsIntegral.isIntegral (R := R) x).choose_spec.1

/-- The chosen annihilating polynomial of `x` vanishes at `x`. -/
theorem annih_aeval (x : S) : Polynomial.aeval x (annih R S x) = 0 :=
  (Algebra.IsIntegral.isIntegral (R := R) x).choose_spec.2

/-- The monic relation imposed on the variable `X x`: the chosen monic annihilator of `x`,
evaluated at `X x`. -/
def rel (x : S) : MvPolynomial S R := Polynomial.aeval (X x : MvPolynomial S R) (annih R S x)

/-- The monic relation on `X x` holds in `S`. -/
theorem eval_rel (x : S) : eval R S (rel R S x) = 0 := by
  rw [rel, ← Polynomial.aeval_algHom_apply, eval_X, annih_aeval]

/-- The monic relation on `X x` lies in the subalgebra generated by the variables indexed by `s`
when `x ∈ s`. -/
theorem rel_mem_varSubalg {s : Set S} {x : S} (hx : x ∈ s) : rel R S x ∈ varSubalg R S s :=
  Algebra.adjoin_mono (Set.singleton_subset_iff.2 ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ :
      ({X x} : Set (MvPolynomial S R)) ⊆ X '' s)
    (by rw [Algebra.adjoin_singleton_eq_range_aeval]; exact ⟨annih R S x, rfl⟩)

/-- The index type of the approximating system: a finite set of variables together with a
finite set of polynomial relations between them which hold in `S`. -/
def Index : Type (max u v) :=
  {p : Set S × Set (MvPolynomial S R) // p.1.Finite ∧ p.2.Finite ∧
    ∀ g ∈ p.2, g ∈ varSubalg R S p.1 ∧ eval R S g = 0}

namespace Index

/-- Indices are ordered by inclusion of both the variable sets and the relation sets. -/
instance : PartialOrder (Index R S) := Subtype.partialOrder _

/-- The index with no variables and no relations. -/
instance : Nonempty (Index R S) := ⟨⟨(∅, ∅), by simp⟩⟩

/-- The indices are directed: take the unions of the variable sets and of the relation sets. -/
instance : IsDirectedOrder (Index R S) := by
  constructor
  rintro ⟨⟨s, G⟩, hs, hG, hmem⟩ ⟨⟨s', G'⟩, hs', hG', hmem'⟩
  refine ⟨⟨(s ∪ s', G ∪ G'), hs.union hs', hG.union hG', ?_⟩,
    ⟨Set.subset_union_left, Set.subset_union_left⟩,
    ⟨Set.subset_union_right, Set.subset_union_right⟩⟩
  rintro g (hg | hg)
  · exact ⟨varSubalg_mono R S Set.subset_union_left (hmem g hg).1, (hmem g hg).2⟩
  · exact ⟨varSubalg_mono R S Set.subset_union_right (hmem' g hg).1, (hmem' g hg).2⟩

omit [Algebra.IsIntegral R S] in
/-- One index lies below another exactly when its variable set and its relation set are contained
in those of the other. -/
theorem le_iff {i j : Index R S} : i ≤ j ↔ i.1.1 ⊆ j.1.1 ∧ i.1.2 ⊆ j.1.2 := Iff.rfl

/-- The index with the single variable `X y` and no prescribed relations. -/
def singleton (y : S) : Index R S :=
  ⟨({y}, ∅), Set.finite_singleton y, Set.finite_empty, by simp⟩

end Index

variable {R S}

/-- The relations imposed at the index `i`: the prescribed ones together with the monic
relation on each chosen variable. -/
def gens (i : Index R S) : Set (MvPolynomial S R) := i.1.2 ∪ rel R S '' i.1.1

/-- The relation set at an index is finite. -/
theorem gens_finite (i : Index R S) : (gens i).Finite := i.2.2.1.union (i.2.1.image _)

/-- The relation set is monotone in the index. -/
theorem gens_mono {i j : Index R S} (h : i ≤ j) : gens i ⊆ gens j :=
  Set.union_subset_union h.2 (Set.image_mono h.1)

/-- Every relation at an index holds in `S`. -/
theorem eval_eq_zero_of_mem_gens {i : Index R S} {g : MvPolynomial S R} (hg : g ∈ gens i) :
    eval R S g = 0 := by
  obtain hg | ⟨x, _, rfl⟩ := hg
  · exact (i.2.2.2 g hg).2
  · exact eval_rel R S x

/-- The subalgebra of the polynomial ring out of which the index `i` carves its algebra. -/
abbrev subalg (i : Index R S) : Subalgebra R (MvPolynomial S R) := varSubalg R S i.1.1

/-- The relations at an index lie in the subalgebra at that index. -/
theorem gens_subset_subalg (i : Index R S) : gens i ⊆ (subalg i : Set (MvPolynomial S R)) := by
  rintro g (hg | ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩)
  · exact (i.2.2.2 g hg).1
  · exact rel_mem_varSubalg R S hx

omit [Algebra.IsIntegral R S] in
/-- The subalgebra at an index is monotone in the index. -/
theorem subalg_mono {i j : Index R S} (h : i ≤ j) : subalg i ≤ subalg j := varSubalg_mono R S h.1

/-- The ideal of relations at the index `i`. -/
def relIdeal (i : Index R S) : Ideal (subalg i) := Ideal.span (Subtype.val ⁻¹' gens i)

/-- The ideal of relations at an index is finitely generated. -/
theorem relIdeal_fg (i : Index R S) : (relIdeal i).FG :=
  Submodule.fg_span (Set.Finite.preimage Subtype.val_injective.injOn (gens_finite i))

/-- The approximating algebra at the index `i`. -/
abbrev obj (i : Index R S) : Type (max u v) := (subalg i) ⧸ relIdeal i

/-- A relation at the index `i` vanishes in the approximating algebra at `i`. -/
theorem mk_eq_zero_of_mem_gens {i : Index R S} (a : subalg i)
    (ha : (a : MvPolynomial S R) ∈ gens i) : (Ideal.Quotient.mk (relIdeal i)) a = 0 :=
  Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 (Ideal.subset_span ha)

/-- **Each approximating algebra is a finite `R`-module.** It is generated as an `R`-algebra
by the images of the chosen variables, and each of those is integral because the monic relation
on it has been imposed. This is the sectionwise form of [Stacks, Tag 02JJ]. -/
theorem moduleFinite_obj (i : Index R S) : Module.Finite R (obj i) := by
  set Q := Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R (relIdeal i)
  set G : Set (subalg i) := Subtype.val ⁻¹' (X '' i.1.1)
  have hGfin : G.Finite := Set.Finite.preimage Subtype.val_injective.injOn (i.2.1.image _)
  have htop0 : Algebra.adjoin R G = ⊤ := Algebra.adjoin_adjoin_coe_preimage
  have htop : Algebra.adjoin R (Q '' G) = ⊤ := by
    have h := AlgHom.map_adjoin Q G
    rw [htop0, Algebra.map_top] at h
    rw [← h, AlgHom.range_eq_top]
    exact Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_surjective R _
  have hint : ∀ y ∈ Q '' G, IsIntegral R y := by
    rintro _ ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨x, hx, hxa⟩ := ha
    refine ⟨annih R S x, annih_monic R S x, ?_⟩
    rw [← Polynomial.aeval_def, Polynomial.aeval_algHom_apply]
    refine mk_eq_zero_of_mem_gens _ ?_
    rw [← Subalgebra.aeval_coe, ← hxa]
    exact Or.inr ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  have hfin := Algebra.finite_adjoin_of_finite_of_isIntegral (hGfin.image _) hint
  rw [htop] at hfin
  exact Module.Finite.equiv (Subalgebra.topEquiv (R := R) (A := obj i)).toLinearEquiv

/-- **Each approximating algebra is of finite presentation over `R`.** It is a quotient of a
polynomial ring on finitely many variables by a finitely generated ideal. -/
theorem finitePresentation_obj (i : Index R S) : Algebra.FinitePresentation R (obj i) :=
  let := finitePresentation_varSubalg R S i.2.1
  Algebra.FinitePresentation.quotient (relIdeal_fg i)

end Stacks.RingTheory.IntegralColimit

end
